cs225aw@ux1.cso.uiuc.edu (Daniel DuBois) writes:

>I have been unable to change MY alignment at an alter... I pray until my God is
>pissed, then I #offer at an alter, and it still changes the altars alignment to
>my neutral God's.  Can someone more deeply explain the process.  I thought I understood the spoilers.

Praying until your god is angry is NOT the answer.

Ever lovin' spoiler warning:

Praying doesn't affect your alignment.  It only affects your god's attitude
toward you personally.  So making your god angry doesn't change you from
"stridently aligned," it just burns you to a crisp eventually.

How to "stray" from your god, without getting burned:

I've found two ways (in wiz mode) to change my godly status so that offering
at a non-aligned alter will switch me, per the spoilers....

1.  Give lots of money to a priest of the other alignment.  (This one is
    easy, as there is an alter right there.)

2.  Kill peaceful creatures, by answering in the affirmative to the "really
    attack?" prompt.

As a side light, I found that throwing stuff at friendlies to kill them or
make 'em angry didn't seem to change my "alignment" characteristic.  This
has helped me "clean out" a level where I'm hanging out at an alter for
10 or 20,000 moves, without hurting my alignment.  It might damage my luck,
but every 600 moves that heads back to zero anyway.
